    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d830">

                <pb facs="0858" n="756" sameAs="frus:frus1933v03/pg756"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">894.3311/180</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Japanese Ambassador (Debuchi) to the Acting Secretary of
                            State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 100</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-06-17">June 17, 1933</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to my note No. 26, dated
                    February 6, 1933,<anchor n="78" xml:id="d830-f1"/> I have the honor to inform
                    you that the Japanese Government have been much pleased with the courtesy and
                    hospitality which the Government and people of the United States have been good
                    enough to extend to the Japanese Training Squadron which is leaving Honolulu
                    today, the last port of call.</p>
                <p>I may further inform you that the Squadron has been given the most cordial
                    co-operation by the naval officers of the United States at each port of call,
                    which has greatly expedited its activities.</p>
                <pb facs="0859" n="757" xml:id="pg757"/>
                <p>I wish to take this opportunity to express to you the sincere thanks of my
                    Government for the above manifestation of good will and courtesy toward the
                    Squadron.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed>K. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Debuchi</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
